From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: what a program has written goes to the sound server at once, up to 100 ms

A playback stream kept three periods (30 ms) at the sound server and the rest of what the program
had written in winepulse's own buffer, for the timer thread to pass on one period at a time. That
thread waits on the sound server (its timing update) and on the wineserver (the program's event)
every period, and beside a 1080p film decoding those waits came to 20-60 ms: the server ran dry
and Media Player's sound hiccuped where VLC's did not (David's renders, 2026-11-22: 5 to 19
underruns in 40 s; with this, 1). Windows' audio engine takes what a program writes when it writes
it. The target length is now the program's buffer, up to 100 ms, and the stream asks for early
requests in place of an adjusted latency, so the server keeps its own short period (an adjusted
latency made it 30 ms for everything on the graph). After an underrun no more than three periods
of silence go in first, as before.

--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -1065,6 +1065,27 @@
     attr.tlength = period_bytes * 3;
     attr.maxlength = stream->bufsize_frames * pa_frame_size(&stream->ss);
     attr.prebuf = pa_frame_size(&stream->ss);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PULSE_SHORT_TLENGTH
+    /* Stained Glass: what the program has written goes to the sound server at once, as Windows'
+     * audio engine takes it, up to 100 ms. With three periods (30 ms) there, the rest waited in
+     * the local buffer for the timer thread, and the timer thread waits on the sound server
+     * (timing) and the wineserver (the program's event) -- 20 to 60 ms at a time with a film
+     * decoding beside it: the server ran dry and the sound hiccuped (Media Player, David's
+     * renders, 2026-11-22: 5 to 19 underruns in 40 s, VLC none). EARLY_REQUESTS, not
+     * ADJUST_LATENCY: the server keeps its own short period instead of growing it to the
+     * longer buffer (30 ms quantum for everything on the graph). */
+    if (stream->dataflow == eRender)
+    {
+        UINT32 want = pa_bytes_per_second(&stream->ss) / 10;
+        want = min(want, attr.maxlength);
+        want -= want % pa_frame_size(&stream->ss);
+        if (want > attr.tlength)
+        {
+            attr.tlength = want;
+            flags = (flags & ~PA_STREAM_ADJUST_LATENCY) | PA_STREAM_EARLY_REQUESTS;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     dump_attr(&attr);
 
     /* If specific device was requested, use it exactly */
@@ -1417,8 +1438,10 @@
     if (stream->just_underran)
     {
         /* prebuffer with silence if needed */
-        if(stream->pa_held_bytes < bytes){
-            to_write = bytes - stream->pa_held_bytes;
+        /* no more silence than three periods' worth: the server may take up to 100 ms now */
+        UINT32 room = min(bytes, stream->period_bytes * 3);
+        if(stream->pa_held_bytes < room){
+            to_write = room - stream->pa_held_bytes;
             TRACE("prebuffering %u frames of silence\n",
                     (int)(to_write / pa_frame_size(&stream->ss)));
             buf = calloc(1, to_write);
